      "content": "No, ignoring these symptoms is dangerous because sudden blackouts can indicate serious issues like stroke, heart arrhythmia, or severe electrolyte imbalances that fluid might not fix alone. Please seek immediate medical attention at an emergency room to get your blood pressure, glucose, and heart rhythm checked right away. It is crucial not to wait or assume heat is the only cause, as your age increases the risk of life-threatening cardiac events.",
